IMPORT prelude

-- Bus Services Industry Act 2015 (Singapore) -- what is a "bus service" and a "regular route service" (s 2), the licence classes
-- (s 2), unauthorised operation of a bus service (s 11) and of a bus depot or bus interchange (s 22), the 5% controller notice and
-- the 25% / 50% / 75% controller approvals for designated entities (ss 28B, 28F, 28G, 28R), and the conduct of individuals on
-- buses and at bus interchanges (ss 42AA to 42AE, 42AG(2), (3)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/BSIA2015.txt, with amendments
-- to Act 17 of 2025 (in force 23 September 2026) shown. Part 7A (ss 42AA to 42AJ) was inserted by that Act and has been in force
-- for under three weeks at the date of this row.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 9 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the rules an operator, an investor in
-- an operator, or a bus passenger actually meets. Not encoded: the bus services procurement framework (Part 2), the matters the
-- LTA weighs in granting licences (ss 13, 24), licence conditions, transfer and management changes (ss 15 to 21, 26 to 28),
-- designation of entities (s 28E) and the meaning of "associate" and "indirect controller" (ss 28B to 28D), remedial directions
-- (ss 28M to 28Q), step-in and special administration (Parts 5, 5A), enforcement and appeals (Parts 6, 7), arrest (s 42AH),
-- exemptions by Ministerial order (s 46), and anything left to regulations (including "prescribed" dangerous items).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Bus Services Industry Act 2015 -- buses`

§§ `2 -- bus service, regular route service, licence classes`

-- s 2: "bus service" means "a service consisting of the carriage of passengers, for a fare, by buses operated -- (a) at
-- predetermined timetables; and (b) on a fixed route on roads for journeys wholly or partly within Singapore with 2 or more bus
-- stopping points within Singapore". "fare" means "the price payable by an individual passenger".
GIVEN `carries passengers for a fare` IS A BOOLEAN, `runs to a predetermined timetable` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `runs on a fixed route on roads in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `stopping points in Singapore` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a bus service` IF
        `carries passengers for a fare`
    AND `runs to a predetermined timetable`
    AND `runs on a fixed route on roads in Singapore`
    AND `stopping points in Singapore` AT LEAST 2

-- s 2: "regular route service" means a bus service conducted according to predetermined routes and timetables with 2 or more
-- stopping points, "but does not include -- (a) a tourist bus service; (b) a community bus service; (c) a courtesy bus service;
-- or (d) a bus service excluded from this definition by the Minister by order in the Gazette". A community or courtesy service is
-- one "provided for a fare, or for consideration which is limited to the costs" -- so each is still a bus service.
DECLARE ServiceKind IS ONE OF
    `an ordinary scheduled route`
    `a tourist bus service`
    `a community bus service`
    `a courtesy bus service`
    `a service excluded by Ministerial order`

GIVEN `is a bus service` IS A BOOLEAN, `the kind` IS A ServiceKind
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a regular route service` IF
        `is a bus service`
    AND CONSIDER `the kind`
        WHEN `an ordinary scheduled route` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 2: "Class 1 bus service licence" -- "authorising the operation of 10 or more regular route services"; "Class 2 bus service
-- licence" -- "authorising the operation of a single bus service". INFERENCE: the definitions name no class for a licence
-- covering 2 to 9 bus services; the encoding returns `no class defined in s 2` for that case.
DECLARE LicenceClass IS ONE OF
    `Class 1`
    `Class 2`
    `no class defined in s 2`

GIVEN `regular route services authorised` IS A NUMBER, `bus services authorised` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LicenceClass
`the licence class` MEANS
    IF `regular route services authorised` AT LEAST 10 THEN `Class 1`
    ELSE IF `bus services authorised` EQUALS 1 THEN `Class 2` ELSE `no class defined in s 2`

§§ `11 -- unauthorised operation of a bus service`

-- s 2: "operate", for a bus service, means "to control or direct the operations of the bus service ... but does not include --
-- (i) merely arranging for the registration of a bus; (ii) merely driving a bus; or (iii) merely maintaining or arranging for the
-- maintenance of a bus".
-- s 11(1): "A person must not operate in Singapore a bus service unless -- (a) ... authorised ... by a bus service licence; (b) ...
-- exempt ...; (c) the person is the LTA; or (d) the person (called ... a bus service subcontractor) is authorised to do so by
-- contract with a person referred to in paragraph (a) or (b)."
DECLARE BusRole IS ONE OF
    `controls or directs the bus service`
    `merely drives a bus`
    `merely registers a bus`
    `merely maintains a bus`

DECLARE Authority IS ONE OF
    `a bus service licence`
    `an exemption`
    `being the LTA`
    `a subcontract with a licensee or exempt person`
    `no authority`

GIVEN `the role` IS A BusRole
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person operates the bus service` IF
    CONSIDER `the role`
    WHEN `controls or directs the bus service` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `is a bus service` IS A BOOLEAN, `the role` IS A BusRole, `the authority` IS A Authority
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `operating the bus service is an offence under s 11` IF
        `is a bus service`
    AND `the person operates the bus service` `the role`
    AND CONSIDER `the authority`
        WHEN `no authority` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `22 -- unauthorised operation of a bus depot or bus interchange`

-- s 2: "operate", for a bus depot or bus interchange, "does not include ... (i) merely driving a bus; (ii) merely repairing a bus;
-- (iii) merely refuelling a bus ...; (iv) merely charging the battery of a bus" (item (iv) added by Act 17 of 2025).
-- s 22(1): the same four authorities as s 11(1), with a bus depot licence or bus interchange licence in place of a bus service
-- licence.
DECLARE DepotRole IS ONE OF
    `controls or directs the depot or interchange`
    `merely drives a bus there`
    `merely repairs a bus there`
    `merely refuels a bus there`
    `merely charges a bus battery there`

GIVEN `the role` IS A DepotRole, `the authority` IS A Authority
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `operating the depot or interchange is an offence under s 22` IF
        CONSIDER `the role`
        WHEN `controls or directs the depot or interchange` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    AND CONSIDER `the authority`
        WHEN `no authority` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `28B, 28F, 28G -- controllers of designated entities`

-- s 28B(1): a "5% controller" holds, alone or with associates, "5% or more, but less than 25%" of the equity interests, or is in a
-- position to control that share of the voting power; a "25% controller" 25% or more but less than 50%; a "50% controller" 50%
-- or more but less than 75%; a "75% controller" 75% or more.
-- INFERENCE: the bands are tested on one number, the larger of equity held and voting power controlled (with associates). The
-- definitions are framed "or", so a person whose two figures fall in different bands may answer to two of them; the encoding
-- does not model that.
DECLARE Band IS ONE OF
    `below 5%`
    `a 5% controller`
    `a 25% controller`
    `a 50% controller`
    `a 75% controller`

GIVEN `percent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Band
`the controller band` MEANS
    IF `percent` AT LEAST 75 THEN `a 75% controller`
    ELSE
        IF `percent` AT LEAST 50 THEN `a 50% controller`
        ELSE
            IF `percent` AT LEAST 25 THEN `a 25% controller`
            ELSE
                IF `percent` AT LEAST 5 THEN `a 5% controller` ELSE `below 5%`

GIVEN `the band` IS A Band
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the band rank` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the band`
    WHEN `below 5%` THEN 0
    WHEN `a 5% controller` THEN 1
    WHEN `a 25% controller` THEN 2
    WHEN `a 50% controller` THEN 3
    OTHERWISE 4

-- s 28F(1): "If a person becomes a 5% controller of a designated entity on or after the effective designation date as a result of
-- an increase in the holding of equity interest, or in the voting power controlled, by that person or any associate of that
-- person, that person must within 7 days after becoming the 5% controller give written notice to the LTA of that fact."
-- Read literally, a person who goes from below 5% straight to 25% or more never "becomes a 5% controller" (the band stops at
-- "less than 25%"), so s 28F is not engaged -- s 28G is.
GIVEN `percent before` IS A NUMBER, `percent after` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a 5% controller notice is required` IF
        `percent after` GREATER THAN `percent before`
    AND `the band rank` (`the controller band` `percent before`) EQUALS 0
    AND `the band rank` (`the controller band` `percent after`) EQUALS 1

-- s 28F(2): contravening (1) is an offence. (3): a defence to prove the accused "(a) was not aware of the contravention when it
-- occurred; and (b) notified the LTA ... within a period of 14 days after becoming aware". (4): a defence to prove, though aware,
-- that (a) the increase was by an associate, (b) there is "no agreement or arrangement" with that associate, and (c) the accused
-- "notified the LTA of the contravention within a period of 7 days after the contravention". (5): otherwise lack of intent or
-- knowledge is no defence.
GIVEN `notice was required` IS A BOOLEAN, `notified within 7 days of becoming a 5% controller` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `was aware of the contravention when it occurred` IS A BOOLEAN, `days from awareness to notice` IS A NUMBER,
      `the increase was by an associate with no arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN, `days from contravention to notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing to give the 5% controller notice is an offence` IF
        `notice was required`
    AND (NOT `notified within 7 days of becoming a 5% controller`)
    AND (NOT ((NOT `was aware of the contravention when it occurred`) AND `days from awareness to notice` AT MOST 14))
    AND (NOT (`was aware of the contravention when it occurred`
              AND `the increase was by an associate with no arrangement`
              AND `days from contravention to notice` AT MOST 7))

-- s 28G(1): "Except with the prior written approval of the LTA, a person must not -- (a) as a result of an increase ... become a
-- 25% controller, 50% controller or 75% controller ...; or (b) as a result of a decrease ... cease to be a 25% controller, 50%
-- controller or 75% controller". (2): not if the transaction "is entered into before the effective designation date". (8):
-- contravention is an offence; penalty s 28R.
-- So approval is needed on the way DOWN as well as up: selling from 30% to 10% needs the LTA's prior written approval.
GIVEN `percent before` IS A NUMBER, `percent after` IS A NUMBER, `transaction before the effective designation date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `LTA prior approval is required` IF
        (NOT `transaction before the effective designation date`)
    AND (    (    `percent after` GREATER THAN `percent before`
              AND `the band rank` (`the controller band` `percent after`) AT LEAST 2
              AND `the band rank` (`the controller band` `percent after`) GREATER THAN `the band rank` (`the controller band` `percent before`))
         OR  (    `percent after` LESS THAN `percent before`
              AND `the band rank` (`the controller band` `percent before`) AT LEAST 2
              AND `the band rank` (`the controller band` `percent before`) GREATER THAN `the band rank` (`the controller band` `percent after`)))

§§ `42AA -- screening on buses and at bus interchanges`

-- s 42AA(2): "a police officer or an approved person may ask" a bus passenger or entrant to walk through a screening detector, put
-- property through an X-ray machine, allow a hand-held scanner near the property, allow inspection of property, empty a bag, turn
-- out pockets, remove a coat etc. (3): "a police officer or senior approved person may also ask" for "(a) ... a frisk search;
-- (b) ... a hand-held scanner in close proximity to the bus passenger".
-- (8): an "approved person" is one of (a) an LTA officer, (b) uniformed auxiliary police, (c) an employee of a Class 1 operator or
-- bus interchange operator, (d) a security officer engaged by that operator, (e) an outsourced enforcement officer -- each
-- "authorised by the LTA in writing". A "senior approved person" is an approved person who is auxiliary police, such a security
-- officer, or an outsourced enforcement officer. The encoding assumes each listed person holds the LTA's written authorisation.
DECLARE Requester IS ONE OF
    `a police officer`
    `an auxiliary police officer`
    `a security officer engaged by the operator`
    `an outsourced enforcement officer`
    `an employee of the bus operator`
    `an LTA officer`
    `a member of the public`

DECLARE Request IS ONE OF
    `walk through a screening detector`
    `put property through an X-ray machine`
    `open a bag`
    `turn out pockets`
    `undergo a frisk search`
    `be scanned in person with a hand-held scanner`

GIVEN `the requester` IS A Requester
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the requester rank` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the requester`
    WHEN `a police officer` THEN 3
    WHEN `an auxiliary police officer` THEN 2
    WHEN `a security officer engaged by the operator` THEN 2
    WHEN `an outsourced enforcement officer` THEN 2
    WHEN `an employee of the bus operator` THEN 1
    WHEN `an LTA officer` THEN 1
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the requester` IS A Requester, `the request` IS A Request
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the requester may make the request` IF
    CONSIDER `the request`
    WHEN `undergo a frisk search` THEN `the requester rank` `the requester` AT LEAST 2
    WHEN `be scanned in person with a hand-held scanner` THEN `the requester rank` `the requester` AT LEAST 2
    OTHERWISE `the requester rank` `the requester` AT LEAST 1

-- s 42AA(6): refusing or failing "without reasonable excuse" to comply is an offence, fine up to $1,000. (7): "it is not an offence
-- ... to refuse to comply with any request ... made or given by -- (a) a police officer who is not in uniform and who fails to
-- declare his or her office; or (b) an approved person or a senior approved person who fails to declare his or her office and, in
-- the case of an outsourced enforcement officer, who also refuses to produce his or her identification card on demand".
-- Read literally, an outsourced enforcement officer who declares office but refuses to show an identification card can still be
-- obeyed on pain of the offence; the (7)(b) carve-out needs both failures.
GIVEN `the requester` IS A Requester, `in uniform` IS A BOOLEAN, `declared office` IS A BOOLEAN, `refused to show ID card` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `refusal is excused by s 42AA(7)` IF
    CONSIDER `the requester`
    WHEN `a police officer` THEN (NOT `in uniform`) AND (NOT `declared office`)
    WHEN `an outsourced enforcement officer` THEN (NOT `declared office`) AND `refused to show ID card`
    OTHERWISE (NOT `declared office`)

GIVEN `the requester` IS A Requester, `the request` IS A Request, `in uniform` IS A BOOLEAN, `declared office` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `refused to show ID card` IS A BOOLEAN, `has a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `refusing the screening request is an offence` IF
        `the requester may make the request` `the requester` `the request`
    AND (NOT `refusal is excused by s 42AA(7)` `the requester` `in uniform` `declared office` `refused to show ID card`)
    AND (NOT `has a reasonable excuse`)

§§ `42AB -- dangerous items`

-- s 42AB(2): a bus passenger or entrant "must not take a dangerous item on board the bus or into the bus interchange unless ... (he
-- or she) has the express permission of a police officer or an approved person". (3): fine up to $5,000. (4): not an offence "if
-- the individual disposes of the dangerous item before boarding the bus or entering the bus interchange". (5): "dangerous item"
-- means (a) any gun, explosive, noxious substance or weapon within the Guns, Explosives and Weapons Control Act 2021; (b) any
-- petroleum or prescribed flammable material; (c) any hazardous or corrosive substance; (d) anything else prescribed.
-- Section 42AB names a bus and a bus interchange; it does not name a bus depot.
DECLARE Item IS ONE OF
    `a weapon`
    `petroleum`
    `a corrosive substance`
    `a prescribed dangerous item`
    `an ordinary umbrella`

DECLARE Place IS ONE OF
    `a bus`
    `a bus interchange`
    `a bus depot`

GIVEN `the item` IS A Item
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a dangerous item` IF
    CONSIDER `the item`
    WHEN `an ordinary umbrella` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the item` IS A Item, `the place` IS A Place, `had express permission` IS A BOOLEAN, `disposed of it before entering` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `taking the item in is an offence under s 42AB` IF
        `it is a dangerous item` `the item`
    AND CONSIDER `the place`
        WHEN `a bus depot` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE
    AND (NOT `had express permission`)
    AND (NOT `disposed of it before entering`)

§§ `42AD, 42AE -- damage and compensation`

-- s 42AD: any person who "wilfully" removes, destroys or damages anything part of a bus, bus depot or bus interchange commits an
-- offence. s 42AE(1): a person who does the same "whether wilfully or otherwise" is liable "in addition to any penalty" to pay
-- compensation, recoverable by civil action; (2) the criminal court may assess it.
GIVEN `damaged a bus, depot or interchange` IS A BOOLEAN, `did so wilfully` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the damage is an offence under s 42AD` IF
    `damaged a bus, depot or interchange` AND `did so wilfully`

GIVEN `damaged a bus, depot or interchange` IS A BOOLEAN, `did so wilfully` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `compensation is payable under s 42AE` IF
    `damaged a bus, depot or interchange`

§§ `Penalties -- ss 11(2), 22(2), 28R, 42AA(6), 42AB(3), 42AC, 42AD, 42AG(2), (3)`

-- s 11(2)(a): where "the number of bus services operated in contravention is 10 or more regular route services" -- $50,000 or 6
-- months or both, and $5,000 a day continuing; (b) "in any other case" -- $10,000, and $500 a day continuing (no imprisonment).
-- s 22(2): $10,000 or 6 months or both, $500 a day continuing. s 28R (every Part 4A offence): $50,000 or 6 months or both, $5,000 a
-- day continuing. s 42AA(6): $1,000. s 42AB(3): $5,000. s 42AC (wilfully endangering safety): $10,000 or 5 years or both.
-- s 42AD (wilful damage): $200,000 or 12 months or both. s 42AG(2) (obstructing an authorised officer): $5,000 or 12 months or both.
-- s 42AG(3) (refusing or wilfully misstating information): $500.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `s 11 with 10 or more regular route services`
    `s 11 in any other case`
    `s 22`
    `a Part 4A offence`
    `s 42AA refusing screening`
    `s 42AB dangerous item`
    `s 42AC endangering safety`
    `s 42AD wilful damage`
    `s 42AG obstruction`
    `s 42AG refusing information`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `s 11 with 10 or more regular route services` THEN 50000
    WHEN `s 11 in any other case` THEN 10000
    WHEN `s 22` THEN 10000
    WHEN `a Part 4A offence` THEN 50000
    WHEN `s 42AA refusing screening` THEN 1000
    WHEN `s 42AB dangerous item` THEN 5000
    WHEN `s 42AC endangering safety` THEN 10000
    WHEN `s 42AD wilful damage` THEN 200000
    WHEN `s 42AG obstruction` THEN 5000
    OTHERWISE 500

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `s 11 with 10 or more regular route services` THEN 6
    WHEN `s 22` THEN 6
    WHEN `a Part 4A offence` THEN 6
    WHEN `s 42AC endangering safety` THEN 60
    WHEN `s 42AD wilful damage` THEN 12
    WHEN `s 42AG obstruction` THEN 12
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the daily fine for a continuing offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `s 11 with 10 or more regular route services` THEN 5000
    WHEN `s 11 in any other case` THEN 500
    WHEN `s 22` THEN 500
    WHEN `a Part 4A offence` THEN 5000
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `regular route services operated without authority` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Offence
`the s 11 penalty tier` MEANS
    IF `regular route services operated without authority` AT LEAST 10 THEN `s 11 with 10 or more regular route services`
    ELSE `s 11 in any other case`
